{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, serve a package repository whose packages and metadata are stored locally.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A signed RHEL 10 RPM and repository metadata were created under /srv/localrepo, exposed through an enabled HTTP service on port 8080, and successfully retrieved with matching local and served checksums. The service and repository recovered after the observed reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f5b238736b744501","cmd-8da37e58413e4191","cmd-82656f7a7f3e48cf","cmd-5090bf1857c74f56","cmd-d7455c7e19544fe6","cmd-bce83fdab76b4146","cmd-7cc568bc8aa640e9"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Install a package from the local repository while the usual remote repositories are unavailable to the package manager.","status":"satisfied","summary":"BaseOS and AppStream were disabled, leaving only local-offline enabled. DNF then installed tree from @local-offline, while an absent remote-only package could not be resolved. A post-restart reinstall again used local-offline successfully.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dab269725aaa4095","cmd-d939e8b9f0e94d2b","cmd-a10b640197814bca","cmd-962d3493c8fd4439","cmd-7cc568bc8aa640e9"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Preserve the installed operating-system release and kernel.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The baseline and final observations consistently show RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0; the same kernel remained installed and running after reboot.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:platform","cmd-eb69d06c3266455f","cmd-bce83fdab76b4146","cmd-7cc568bc8aa640e9","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The repository tooling and target package were native el10 packages, the RPM was Red Hat-signed, and the server used the platform's installed Python 3.12 runtime.","evidence_ids":["cmd-6c28636fe2564e93","cmd-85c9f6510e084f65","cmd-f5b238736b744501","cmd-7cc568bc8aa640e9"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"State-changing actions had clear roles: installing repository tooling, creating repository content and configuration, enabling the hardened service and firewall access, disabling remote repositories, installing the target package, completing the mandatory reboot protocol, and cleaning caches. One unnecessary bounded mutation occurred: cmd-016c93f587304f61 attempted an already-installed jq package and refreshed local metadata, so it did not provide the intended negative-control evidence; package state was unchanged and cache residue was subsequently removed by cmd-962d3493c8fd4439 and cmd-9272bf966e484963. No failed services, damaged package state, abandoned reboot unit, or unexplained temporary residue remained. The restart evidence is complete: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, changed boot ID, recovered services/data, and lifecycle cross-checks all agree.","evidence_ids":["cmd-016c93f587304f61","cmd-d7455c7e19544fe6","cmd-48a3d919e8684475","cmd-47cafc78ba6b4bd2","cmd-bce83fdab76b4146","cmd-9272bf966e484963","cmd-7cc568bc8aa640e9","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Node1 serves a functional local repository, tree was installed through it with the usual remote repositories disabled, and the RHEL release and kernel were preserved. The mandatory node-restart protocol was directly and coherently demonstrated.","limitations":["Remote unavailability during installation was demonstrated at the DNF configuration and resolution level by disabling BaseOS/AppStream and failing to resolve a remote-only package; no transport-layer network outage was captured at that exact time."]}
